Use your image generation tool to create exactly ONE image: a landscape-format (1536x1024) scene of a rainy city street at night under dark, heavy, billowing storm clouds that fill the upper half of the image, a skyline of building silhouettes with a few lit windows, and wet reflective pavement in the lower half, no lightning bolt drawn. The street lamps must be placed the way real ones are: identical cast-iron lamp posts standing in one row at the edge of the sidewalk, on the curb, evenly spaced about 30 metres apart, so that in perspective only a few are visible (a large near one, a much smaller one further along, a tiny one in the distance); none stands in the middle of a walkway or road, in front of a doorway or blocking stairs. The wet pavement shows warm reflected streaks only directly below the lamps and lit windows, with cool sky reflections elsewhere. Do not draw any rain streaks or raindrops (the rain is added later); the scene is wet, dark and stormy. Detailed painterly pixel art in the style of classic early-1990s adventure game backgrounds, rich color with smooth dithered gradients, moderate contrast, no large pure-white areas (a translucent menu panel with text sits over most of it). Keep every important element inside the central 85% of the width, because the sides will be cropped to 4:3. No text, no frame, no border, no vignette, no watermark. Save the generated image into the current directory as thunderstorm-city.png (copy it from wherever the tool writes it, do not resize or edit it). Print only the saved path. Do nothing else.
